          ],
          "documentation": "UI supplies unique transactionId. Require customer and >=1 art at construction. Incomplete iff transactionDate==null. Complete assigns date and stored art+shipping total once. Completed transactions cannot be edited or removed. No public setters for id/date/price. updateCustomer/addArt/removeArt reject completed state; removeArt must retain >=1 art. Defensive getters: customer-data copy, structural art-list copy, Date copy; immutable Art objects may be shared. formatForPrint returns transaction data; toString formats data for persistence. Reconstructed completed records do not repeat completion. Art IDs in artPieces must be unique; constructor/addArt reject duplicates before mutation. Invalid add/remove/edit actions preserve the existing transaction.",
          "attributes": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLAttribute",
